  "health_insurance": "Health Insurance",
  "insurance_intro_title": "A Health Insurance Service That Sets Us Apart",
  "insurance_intro_body": "The system offers an integrated health insurance service for all citizens, plus hospital staff and their first-degree relatives (spouse, children, parents). This turns the system from an internal operations tool into a service platform that creates direct value for the community and the facility alike, giving the hospital an additional revenue stream (subscription premiums) while reducing the financial burden on patients.",
  "insurance_model_title": "Adopted Model: South Korea's National Health Insurance Service (NHIS)",
  "insurance_model_body": "This module is inspired by South Korea's NHIS, one of the most successful universal health insurance models worldwide: it achieved full population coverage in just 12 years through mandatory subsidized contributions, and proved able to cut patients' out-of-pocket costs to under 20% compared to peer countries, while maintaining high care quality and public satisfaction. We applied the same core principles: a fixed coverage percentage on every invoice, an annual cap protecting against catastrophic bills, and automatic linkage between subscription status and billing.",
  "benefit_universal_title": "Coverage for Every Category",
  "benefit_universal_body": "Separate plans for the general public, hospital staff (as a work benefit), and their first-degree relatives - each with coverage rates suited to that group.",
  "benefit_cap_title": "Protection from Catastrophic Bills",
  "benefit_cap_body": "An annual coverage cap per member guarantees continued support even for major health events, following the Korean NHIS model.",
  "benefit_staff_title": "An Exclusive Staff Perk",
  "benefit_staff_body": "90% coverage with no monthly premium for all hospital staff - a strong tool for attracting and retaining medical and technical talent.",
  "future_suggestions_title": "Suggestions to Develop the Service Further",
  "suggestion_1": "A digital insurance card with a barcode (reusing the barcode system already in the app) for quick scanning at reception instead of manual entry.",
  "suggestion_2": "A pre-authorization workflow for costly procedures and tests before they are performed.",
  "suggestion_3": "Bundled family registration: enroll a staff member and all first-degree relatives in one flow instead of one by one.",
  "suggestion_4": "Automatic renewal reminders before a subscription expires, linked to an in-app notification for the employee.",
  "suggestion_5": "A KPI dashboard indicator showing member count, total monthly covered amounts, and per-plan utilization rate.",
